From: rawaha-e <219735494+rawaha-e@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:07:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] brltty-genkey: try the next method when one fails

The script runs with "set -e". When a method fails, try() returns the
failing status, which ends the script right there. On a system without
mcookie, the first method tried, brltty-genkey exits with status 127
and never gets to /dev/urandom.

Have try() return success when the method fails, so the loop moves on
to the next one as intended.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 brltty-genkey | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/brltty-genkey b/brltty-genkey
index 43b9584..664e4b2 100755
--- a/brltty-genkey
+++ b/brltty-genkey
@@ -38,6 +38,8 @@ try() {
       logTask "key generated"
       exit 0
    }
+
+   return 0
 }
 
 [ -n "${keyFile}" ] || keyFile="${defaultKeyFile}"
